29
00:01:49,050 --> 00:01:56,390
Alright, but you're probably wondering what is a New Year's resolution so why don't we take a look at this word and many more on Language Takeaway.

30
00:01:58,840 --> 00:01:59,190
Language Takeaway.

31
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:03,320
Okay, so New Year's resolution, let's break this phrase down.

32
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:05,280
The first phrase is New Year's.

33
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:24,000
So the New Year is January 1st in the West and it is celebrated on the 31st of December at night when the clock changes to the New Year and a New Year's resolution, remember that S there, is something that you want to do or to change in the New Year.

34
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:24,800
It's a fresh start.

35
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:30,840
Okay, so you pretty much, the verb that you use there is to resolve to do something.

36
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:36,600
So my New Year's resolution is to go to the gym every day.

37
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:37,860
It's like a promise to yourself.

38
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:42,000
Right, so and this is very common right among Americans.

39
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,660
They try and because it's a New Year, it's a fresh start so they want to start doing something great.

40
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:53,370
Exactly, we can talk about this at the end but a lot of companies try to use this to sell Americans stupid things so we'll get there in a minute.

41
00:02:53,640 --> 00:03:00,240
But the two people in this dialogue are talking about the idea of spending more time with friends and family.

42
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:05,400
And the other person says, well sometimes it's hard to do that because you have to provide your family with goods and services.

43
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:11,140
This phrase goods and services is very common especially in economics and sociology.

44
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:12,340
So what does this mean?

45
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:13,420
And they go together, right?

46
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:21,720
So goods are tangible items, things that you buy, you know like food or you know clothes, a TV, etc.

47
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:22,720
Stuff.

48
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:23,720
Stuff.

49
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:29,440
And services of course are other things like for example going to the doctor or the dentist or any other service you get.

50
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:32,620
So service usually includes another person doing something for you.

51
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:38,480
But you might not actually get something physical like a TV if you pay for it.

52
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:44,280
So goods and services, it's included in this phrase always goods and services.

53
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:44,460
Very good.

54
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:51,040
And well moving on as we mentioned with the New Year's resolution, we had that verb there, to resolve.

55
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:55,360
So what does it mean if I want to resolve?

56
00:03:55,360 --> 00:04:01,340
Okay well to resolve as we said is to decide or to promise yourself to do something.

57
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,640
So it's a decision that you don't want to change your mind about.

58
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:09,980
For example, I, this year, I've resolved to quit smoking.

59
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:14,120
That means I've made a decision for myself and I'm going to do it.

60
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:15,460
Okay, very good.

61
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:16,640
It's very strong.

62
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,780
And not to be confused with like to solve, right?

63
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,000
It has no real relation there, right?

64
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:30,860
No, resolve, to resolve to do something is to have a strong passion or interest in doing something for yourself or changing an action.

65
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:31,640
Very good.

66
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:35,420
And well our last word for language takeaway is brand new.

67
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:37,620
A brand new, something that's brand new.

68
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:41,240
Brand new, so buy a brand new car.

69
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:42,690
Come down to Captain's car lot.

70
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:45,350
So brand new is something we hear a lot in marketing.

71
00:04:45,730 --> 00:04:49,150
It's also something that, well these words just go together very often.

72
00:04:49,770 --> 00:04:54,290
And something is new, okay, you just bought it or it just came out.

73
00:04:54,810 --> 00:04:57,690
But something that's brand new is really fresh, really new.

74
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:01,960
So brand new, a brand new car, a brand new watch, etc.

75
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:02,670
A brand new movie.

76
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:06,430
A brand new movie or brand new cereal.

77
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:08,680
Have you ever tried it?

78
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:08,890
Very good.

